te Galois group as functors on FinExt_K satisfying certain property. Show that FinExt_K simeq FinExt_K' induces an isomorphism Gal_K simeq Gal_K'.", "label": "Relate Galois Group with Category of Finite Field Extensions", "env_name": "definition", "index": 1}, {"id": "D2", "type": "definition", "name": "Perfectoid Fields", "statement": "Let K be a topological field. We say that K is a perfectoid field if and only if the following conditions are satisfied:\\\\ (a) the topology on K is induced by a valuation \\| cdot \\| : K to R_ge0, and K is complete for this topology;\\\\ (b) there exists a non-unit pi in O_K such that p in pi^p O_K;\\\\ (c) every element of O_K/pO_K is a pth-power.", "origin": "paper", "tags": [], "subclass": null, "rigor": null, "raw_latex": "\n    \\label{Perfectoid Field}\n    \n    \n\n    Let $K$ be a topological field. We say that $K$ is a \\emph{perfectoid field} if and only if the following conditions are satisfied:\\\\\n    (a) the topology on K is induced by a valuation $\\| \\cdot \\| : K \\to \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge0}$, and $K$ is complete for this topology;\\\\\n    (b) there exists a non-unit $\\pi \\in \\mathcal{O}_K$ such that $p \\in \\pi^p \\mathcal{O}_K$;\\\\\n    (c) every element of $\\mathcal{O}_K/p\\mathcal{O}_K$ is a $p$th-power.\n", "clean_text": "Let K be a topological field. We say that K is a perfectoid field if and only if the following conditions are satisfied:\\\\ (a) the topology on K is induced by a valuation \\| cdot \\| : K to R_ge0, and K is complete for this topology;\\\\ (b) there exists a non-unit pi in O_K such that p in pi^p O_K;\\\\ (c) every element of O_K/pO_K is a pth-power.", "label": "Perfectoid Field", "env_name": "definition", "index": 2}, {"id": "D3", "type": "definition", "name": null, "statement": "There is an equivalence of category (-)^flat : left \\ Perfectoid fields over K right \\ & to left \\ Perfectoid fields over K^flat right \\ : (-)^\\# \\\\ L & mapsto L^flat", "origin": "paper", "tags": [], "subclass": null, "rigor": null, "raw_latex": "\n    \\label{Tilting Functor}\n    \n\n    There is an equivalence of category\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (-)^\\flat : \\left \\{ \\text{Perfectoid fields over } K \\right \\} & \\to \\left \\{ \\text{Perfectoid fields over } K^\\flat \\right \\} : (-)^\\# \\\\\n        L & \\mapsto L^\\flat\n    \\end{align*}\n\n", "clean_text": "There is an equivalence of category (-)^flat : left \\ Perfectoid fields over K right \\ & to left \\ Perfectoid fields over K^flat right \\ : (-)^\\# \\\\ L & mapsto L^flat", "label": "Tilting Functor", "env_name": "definition", "index": 3}, {"id": "E1", "type": "equation", "name": null, "statement": "(-)^flat : left \\ Perfectoid fields over K right \\ & to left \\ Perfectoid fields over K^flat right \\ : (-)^\\# \\\\ L & mapsto L^flat", "origin": "paper", "tags": [], "subclass": null, "rigor": null, "raw_latex": "\\begin{align*}\n        (-)^\\flat : \\left \\{ \\text{Perfectoid fields over } K \\right \\} & \\to \\left \\{ \\text{Perfectoid fields over } K^\\flat \\right \\} : (-)^\\# \\\\\n        L & \\mapsto L^\\flat\n    \\end{align*}", "clean_text": "(-)^flat : left \\ Perfectoid fields over K right \\ & to left \\ Perfectoid fields over K^flat right \\ : (-)^\\# \\\\ L & mapsto L^flat", "env_name": "align*", "index": 1}, {"id": "T1", "type": "theorem", "name": null, "statement": "Let M be a finite extension of K^flat. (M is automatically a perfectoid field. add this theorem) Then its untilt M^\\# is of the same degree.", "origin": "paper", "tags": [], "subclass": null, "rigor": null, "assumptions": ["Let M be a finite extension of K^flat.", "(M is automatically a perfectoid field."], "conclusions": ["add this theorem) Then its untilt M^\\# is of the same degree."], "raw_latex": "\n    \\label{untilt_same_degree}\n    \n    \n\n    Let $M$ be a finite extension of $K^\\flat$. ($M$ is automatically a perfectoid field. add this theorem) Then its untilt $M^\\#$ is of the same degree.